Route normal OSC 52 writes to the default clipboard so browser clients receive
terminal copy requests. Explicit clipboard types use an in-memory map in
BrowserClipboardService, so sending the normal 'c' destination as 'clipboard'
never reaches navigator.clipboard.writeText. Keep PRIMARY selection and reads
unchanged.

Reproduce in a browser terminal by running:
  printf '\033]52;c;Q0xJUEJPQVJEX1RFU1Q=\007'
Pasting into another application should yield CLIPBOARD_TEST. Without the fix,
the browser clipboard retains its previous value. Covered end-to-end in
 test/e2e/terminal.test.ts, with destination mapping cases in the VS Code patch.

